# .dockerignore standards (Node.js full-stack)

Keep build context small and secret-free. Applies to all three Dockerfiles in this repo.

## Required exclusions

```dockerignore
# ✅ GOOD — minimum set for this workshop repo
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.github/
.env*
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
```

```dockerignore
# ❌ BAD — missing secrets or shipping host node_modules
# (no .dockerignore, or only node_modules)
```

## Keep for builds (do NOT ignore)

These are needed when `COPY . .` runs `npm run build`:

- `vite.config.ts`
- `esbuild.config.js`
- `tailwind.config.js`, `postcss.config.js`
- `tsconfig.json`
- `src/`

Use negation when broad patterns would exclude them:

```dockerignore
*.config.js
!vite.config.ts
!esbuild.config.js
!tailwind.config.js
!postcss.config.js
!tsconfig.json
```

## Optional exclusions (this repo)

```dockerignore
*.md
compose.yml
Taskfile.yml
nodejs-sample-kubernetes.yaml
```

Docs and Compose files are not needed inside the image.

## Security notes

- **Never** allow `.env` or `.env.local` in the build context — use Compose/runtime env instead.
- Excluding `.git/` prevents accidental history leaks and speeds builds.
- Excluding `coverage/` and `**/__tests__/**` is optional; tests still run via `Dockerfile.test` with full `COPY . .` if not ignored.
- Review `COPY . .` after editing `.dockerignore`; a new secret file at repo root must be listed.

## Avoid

- Ignoring `package-lock.json` (breaks reproducible `npm ci`).
- Ignoring `esbuild.config.js` or `vite.config.ts` (build fails).
- Copying `node_modules` from host instead of installing in-container.
